        {
          "expected_id": "n03-f1",
          "location": "src/editor.rs:35-39",
          "issue_type": "Correctness",
          "description": "`before` is not a snapshot of the document. `Doc` is a handle whose lines live behind an `Rc<RefCell<Vec<String>>>` and whose `Clone` is derived, so `self.doc.clone()` yields a second handle onto the same buffer. `self.doc.apply(&op)` mutates the buffer both handles share, and the two checksums are therefore equal after every operation, including operations that changed the text. `dirty` is now never set, `save_if_needed` always returns false, and edits are silently never written out -- the opposite of the intended narrowing, which was meant to skip only the no-op operations."
        }
      ],
      "withheld": 0
